# Waterfall hardware support report

Maintain the official-device waterfall support matrix whenever support assumptions change.

## Artifacts

- [`reports/waterfall-hardware-support.json`](reports/waterfall-hardware-support.json) — machine-readable matrix
- [`reports/waterfall-hardware-support.html`](reports/waterfall-hardware-support.html) — standalone HTML twin
- Canvas: `waterfall-hardware-support.canvas.tsx` (managed canvases dir)

## When to regenerate

In the **same turn**, run:

```sh
python3 contrib/waterfall/tools/gen-hardware-support-report.py
```

whenever any of these change:

1. [`SUPPORTED_DEVICES.md`](SUPPORTED_DEVICES.md) (add/remove/rename devices or status)
2. Waterfall capability logic in [`contrib/waterfall/src/usr/share/ucode/waterfall.uc`](contrib/waterfall/src/usr/share/ucode/waterfall.uc) (`isFocusBoard`, chipset/FFT paths, supportStatus)
3. Package version in [`contrib/waterfall/build.sh`](contrib/waterfall/build.sh) (so the report stamps the current `-v`)
4. Classification rules inside [`contrib/waterfall/tools/gen-hardware-support-report.py`](contrib/waterfall/tools/gen-hardware-support-report.py)

## Categories (do not rename casually)

- **Supported now** — current package can probe/capture on this hardware class
- **Possible with updates** — feasible with more package/firmware work
- **Cannot support** — no viable spectral waterfall path (e.g. HaLow, x86/VM)

Focus devices called out in the report: Rocket M5, PowerBeam M5/500, PowerBeam 5AC 500, hAP ac lite.
